  "id": "lamarckism",
  "term": "Lamarckism",
  "definition": "Lamarckism is a historical biological view that changes produced in an individual by use or by the environment in one generation help shape similar inherited variations in the next. In this usage, it is linked with the idea that evolution follows a directed course rather than occurring only through chance variation.",
